rson facing Johnson County legislator Cindy Holscher. Recent polls from Emerson and a Republican-affiliated firm show Masterson up about seven to eight points, driven by independent voters leaning his way, though an August Democratic-sponsored poll had Holscher narrowly ahead. Five of six expert ratings call the race Lean R, with one calling it a Tossup.\n\nPrediction markets give Holscher roughly a three-in-ten chance. The race has featured sharp exchanges over taxes, data centers, and vouchers, and Holscher has attacked Masterson for skipping debates. The state's Republican lean and the absence of Kelly on the ballot make the GOP favorite, but the polling is thin enough that a strong debate performance or shifting independent sentiment could tighten the race.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1817, "margin": -4.47}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.161, "margin": -5.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1643, "margin": -5.5}]}